<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia manufacturing output prices rose in Feb.</title>
<headline>Australia manufacturing output prices rose in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's manufacturing output prices rose 0.2 percent in February to be 0.6 percent up on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Prices rose 0.3 percent in January for a 0.5 percent year-on-year rise. </p>
<p>Manufacturing output prices (base 1988/89):</p>
<p>				    Index   mth/mth pct  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    February		    122.3     +0.2	 +0.6</p>
<p>    January		     122.0     +0.3	 +0.5</p>
<p>    February 1996	     121.6     +0.2	 +2.1</p>
<p>Note - The bureau said price increases for basic metal products and petrol were the main contributors to the increase in the index.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
